## Walking on the bridge and surfing under it already work - those come from
## the elevation in the map data (confirmed on hardware 2026-09-19, Route 110).
## What was missing is fishing, wild encounters while surfing, and the
## battle background.
##
## All three callers have the same shape and compare against 1:
##
##     LDRB/LSL/LSR r0 ...
##     BL   08059814        ->   SUB r0,#0x6F
##                               NOP            (MOV r8,r8)
##     LSL  r0,r0,#24
##     LSR  r0,r0,#24
##     CMP  r0,#1
##     BEQ/BNE ...
##
## 0x70 becomes exactly 1, so it passes; every other value can never become 1,
## so it always falls to "not a bridge". No out-of-range read is possible.
##
## Because only ONE value can pass, every Hoenn bridge tile is mapped to 0x70
## (see EXTRA_BEHAVIOR_MAP). Vanilla Kanto uses 0 cells of 0x70.
##
##   0807F4A6 BattleSetup_GetTerrainId -> battle background is water
##   08082988 wild_encounter           -> wild battles while surfing
##   080A26CC CanFish (item_use)       -> fishing from the bridge
